.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH proxmox-mcp-rs 1  "proxmox-mcp-rs 0.3.35" 
.SH NAME
proxmox\-mcp\-rs
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBproxmox\-mcp\-rs\fR [\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-H\fR|\fB\-\-host\fR] [\fB\-p\fR|\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-u\fR|\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-P\fR|\fB\-\-password\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-token\-name\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-token\-value\fR] [\fB\-k\fR|\fB\-\-no\-verify\-ssl\fR] [\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-file\-enable\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-filename\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-rotate\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-server\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-http\-host\fR] [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-http\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-http\-auth\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-lazy\-mode\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Config file path
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_CONFIG\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-host\fR \fI<HOST>\fR
Proxmox Host (e.g., 192.168.1.10)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_HOST\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR
Proxmox Port (default: 8006)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_PORT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-u\fR, \fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
Proxmox User (e.g., root@pam)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_USER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-password\fR \fI<PASSWORD>\fR
Proxmox Password
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_PASSWORD\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-token\-name\fR \fI<TOKEN_NAME>\fR
API Token Name (e.g., mytoken)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_TOKEN_NAME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-token\-value\fR \fI<TOKEN_VALUE>\fR
API Token Value (UUID)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_TOKEN_VALUE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-no\-verify\-ssl\fR
Disable SSL verification (for self\-signed certs)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_NO_VERIFY_SSL\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR [default: info]
Log level (error, warn, info, debug, trace)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_LOG_LEVEL\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\-enable\fR
Enable logging to a file
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_LOG_FILE_ENABLE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-dir\fR \fI<LOG_DIR>\fR [default: .]
Log file directory
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_LOG_DIR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-filename\fR \fI<LOG_FILENAME>\fR [default: proxmox\-mcp\-rs.log]
Log filename prefix
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_LOG_FILENAME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-rotate\fR \fI<LOG_ROTATE>\fR [default: daily]
Log rotation strategy (daily, hourly, never)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_LOG_ROTATE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-server\-type\fR \fI<SERVER_TYPE>\fR
Server type (stdio or http)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_SERVER_TYPE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-http\-host\fR \fI<HTTP_HOST>\fR
HTTP Host (only for http type)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_HTTP_HOST\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-http\-port\fR \fI<HTTP_PORT>\fR
HTTP Port (only for http type)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_HTTP_PORT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-http\-auth\-token\fR \fI<HTTP_AUTH_TOKEN>\fR
HTTP Auth Token (only for http type)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_HTTP_AUTH_TOKEN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-lazy\-mode\fR
Enable Lazy Loading mode (starts with minimal tools)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBPROXMOX_LAZY_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
proxmox\-mcp\-rs\-completions(1)
Generate shell completion scripts
.TP
proxmox\-mcp\-rs\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.3.35
